# Project Rules

## Language

- **Code stays English.** All code, identifiers, file names, comments, commit
  messages, and assistant responses MUST be in English.
- **Site content is multilingual.** User-facing content may be localized into
  the supported locales: English (`en`, canonical source), Danish (`da`),
  German (`de`), and Swedish (`sv`). English is the source of truth; the other
  locales are translated from it.
- URL slugs are English by default; localized slugs are allowed only via the
  slug-pair mechanism in `src/data/lang.ts`.
- Product and brand names (the RoomAlyzer lines and product names) are NOT
  translated — they stay identical across all locales, with **one approved
  exception**: "Water detector" is **"Wasserdetektor"** in German (`de`).
  Per-locale name overrides live in `src/data/sensorCategories.ts`
  (`localizedSensorName`); do not add others without explicit approval.
- When adding new content, write the English version first, then provide the
  translations (or rely on the English fallback) for the other locales.

### Localization content rules (names, places, standards)

When translating or localizing copy (`da` / `de` / `sv`), follow these rules
in addition to the product-name rules above:

| Category | Rule |
|----------|------|
| **Person names** | Never translate (team, quotes, bylines). |
| **Customer org / brand names** | Use the **official registered name** (e.g. `Erzdiözese Freiburg`, `Evangelische Kirche in Hessen und Nassau`, `Dansk Industri`, `Sweco`). Do not paraphrase into another language. |
| **Danish municipalities (customers)** | Use **locale-appropriate government label + place name**: `Varde Kommune` (da), `Gemeinde Varde` (de), `Varde kommun` (sv). Keep geographic spelling (`Solrød`, `Holbæk`). No erroneous possessives (e.g. not `Gribskovs kommun`). |
| **Geographic proper nouns** | Keep official spelling (`Freiburg`, `Roskilde`, `Hessen`). |
| **Standards and acronyms** | Keep the **official identifier** unchanged: `EN 15757`, `GDPR`, `CO₂`, `ISO 27001`, `MQTT`, `BR18`, `DGNB`, etc. Translate only the explanatory prose around them. |
| **Locale-specific regulations** | May name local rules (`BR18`, `APV`, `EHF`/`PEPPOL`) but on non-DK locales add jurisdiction context or “or your local equivalent” where relevant. |
| **Glossary terms** | Keep `term` and `anchor` as canonical identifiers; translate `short` and `detail` only. |
| **Sensor `heroTitle`** | Do not add “Sensor”/“sensor” suffixes in i18n overlays; use English catalogue titles + `localizedSensorName()` for approved DE exceptions only. |

## Excluded personnel

- **Dennis Knudsen** must not appear anywhere on this website — team
  pages, contact lists, press material, case studies, blog posts, metadata,
  or generated content. He no longer works at IoT Fabrikken. If his name
  appears in existing content, remove it. Do not add him back unless the
  user explicitly revokes this rule.

## RoomAlyzer product portfolio (official)

The authoritative product list uses **four lines only**. Do not publish Series A/B/C,
vendor names (e.g. Disruptive Technologies, Efento), or other alternate groupings.

| Line | Products |
|------|----------|
| **RoomAlyzer Air** | CO2, Full+, Humidity, Mini+, Mini+ PIR, Outdoor, Temperature |
| **RoomAlyzer Space** | Desk, Motion, Open/Close, Touch |
| **RoomAlyzer Water** | Water detector, Water rope |
| **Miscellaneous** | Cloud connector, Range Extender and Bracket |

- **Full+ PIR** is RoomAlyzer Air but must **not** appear on the site until explicitly approved.
- **When adding a new product**, ask which RoomAlyzer line it belongs to before updating the catalogue.
- Product sheet PDFs are localized. Sources under `Productsheets/{EN,DE,DK}/`;
  served via `scripts/sync-product-sheets.mjs` into:
  - English (canonical): `/downloads/product-sheets/{slug}.pdf`
  - German: `/downloads/product-sheets/de/{slug}.pdf`
  - Danish: `/downloads/product-sheets/da/{slug}.pdf`
  Swedish sheets do not exist yet, so `sv` pages fall back to the English PDF.
  Use `productSheetPath(slug, lang)` (`src/data/sensorCategories.ts`) to resolve
  the correct URL. Re-run the sync script whenever the source PDFs change.
- Catalogue data: [`src/data/hubs/sensors.ts`](src/data/hubs/sensors.ts).

## Event landing pages

**Canonical template:** [`src/pages/[lang]/events/archivistica.astro`](src/pages/[lang]/events/archivistica.astro).
Every event detail landing must follow the same page structure and section order.
**Colours and accent tokens are per event** (e.g. Archivistica navy/coral/sky;
WORKTECH zinc/violet) — reuse layout, spacing, and components; only swap the theme.

### Required files when adding an event

- Registry: [`src/data/events.ts`](src/data/events.ts) — `siteEvents`, `eventAssets`,
  `LOCALE_SCOPED_ROUTES`, and redirects in `astro.config.mjs` for non-host locales.
- Hub cards: [`src/data/i18n/events.ts`](src/data/i18n/events.ts) — Card 1 (active) and
  Card 2 (news) copy per locale.
- Landing copy: `src/data/i18n/{event}.ts` — all hero, section, and CTA strings.
- Images: `src/data/{event}Images.ts` and assets under `public/images/events/{slug}/`.
- Pages: `src/pages/[lang]/events/{slug}.astro` (host locale only) and matching
  `src/pages/[lang]/contact/{slug}.astro`.

### Page structure (fixed order)

1. **Layout** — `suppressHreflang`, `noindex`, `canonicalPath` pinned to the host locale.
2. **Hero** — `align="left"`, `compactTop`, `splitVisual`, `allowVisualOverflow`, `dark`,
   event `darkTone` on `Hero`, `noPattern`; breadcrumb (Home → Events → event); primary CTA
   to event contact, secondary to book demo; visual column: `EventCardActive` with `static`
   (same card as the hub, with hover lift) plus `heroMeta` chips below.
3. **Features** — white band, `SectionIntro`, three-column feature cards with per-event
   `featureStyles`.
4. **Quote** — full-width dark band, decorative quote mark, partner/customer quote block
   (event-themed background and accents).
5. **Testimonials** — white band, three testimonial cards, reference pills, then
   `<LogoMarquee />` (position only — carousel itself stays locked).
6. **Fair / venue photos** — white band, `SectionIntro`, event photo collage.
7. **CtaBand** — `variant="featured"`; primary to event contact (`#kontakt` anchor),
   secondary to book demo.

Do not invent alternate hero layouts (e.g. standalone venue images) or skip sections
without explicit approval. Optional section *content* may differ per event; section
*slots* stay the same.

## General

- Keep changes small and focused.
- Prefer Astro and Tailwind best practices.
- Avoid adding dependencies unless necessary.

## Logo carousel (locked)

The customer logo carousel — the `LogoMarquee.astro` component, its
markup, CSS, JavaScript, the customer roster, the per-customer URLs, and
the logo asset files under `public/logos/` — is **frozen** and must not
be modified in any way (size, spacing, speed, colours, hover effect,
animation, drag behaviour, list contents, ordering, links, or assets).

If a future user request would touch any of the above, you MUST first
ask the user to confirm explicitly that they really want to change the
locked carousel before making the edit. Phrase it as a direct yes/no
confirmation, e.g.: "The logo carousel is locked per project rules — are
you sure you want to change it?"

The only exception is **moving the `<LogoMarquee />` invocation up or
down within a page** (i.e. its vertical position relative to other
sections, with no changes to the component itself). Even this exception
requires explicit confirmation from the user before being applied.
